.\" Generated from wwal.1.scd
.TH "WWAL" "1" "2026-10-24" "wwal 1.0.0" "WayWal Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
wwal - zero-copy Wayland wallpaper, VA-API video, Shadertoy, and Material You client
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBwwal\fR [GLOBAL OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGUMENTS...]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBwwal\fR is the command-line controller for \fBwwald\fR(1), a C23 Wayland wallpaper engine that unifies static DMA-BUF wallpapers, 18 GLES 3.1 compute shader transitions, zero-FFmpeg VA-API hardware video playback, live Shadertoy fragment/compute shaders with PipeWire 64-bin Bark FFT audio reactivity, and sub-millisecond OKLab/CAM16/HCT Material Design 3 color extraction.
.PP
When invoked via a symlink named \fBswww\fR or \fBawww\fR, \fBwwal\fR automatically enables full command-line compatibility with \fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR scripts, pickers, and flags.
.PP
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-j, --json\fR
.RS 4
Format \fBquery\fR, \fBstatus\fR, and \fBstats\fR output as structured JSON.
.RE
.PP
\fB-n, --namespace\fR <NAME>
.RS 4
Connect to the daemon socket namespace \fINAME\fR (default: \fBdefault\fR). Also sets the Wayland layer-shell namespace unless overridden.
.RE
.PP
\fB-v, --verbose\fR
.RS 4
Enable verbose diagnostic output.
.RE
.PP
\fB-V, --version\fR
.RS 4
Print version information and exit.
.RE
.PP
\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS 4
Display usage information and exit.
.RE
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
\fBimg\fR <PATH|-> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Decode and display a static or animated image (PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF, HEIC, JPEG-XL, SVG, BMP, GIF). Pass \fB-\fR to read image bytes from standard input. File descriptors are passed to \fBwwald\fR(1) via \fBSCM_RIGHTS\fR for zero-copy decoding inside the sandbox.
.RE
.PP
\fBvideo\fR <PATH> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Play a hardware-accelerated video wallpaper (MP4, WebM, MKV, GIF) using the zero-FFmpeg MP4/WebM demuxer and VA-API hardware decode pipeline (H.264, HEVC, VP9, AV1).
.RE
.PP
\fBshader\fR <PATH> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Run a live procedural GLSL compute shader (\fB.comp\fR) or multi-pass Shadertoy fragment shader (\fB.frag\fR) on the background layer with automatic \fBinotify\fR(7) hot-reloading.
.RE
.PP
\fBworkshop\fR <list|info|apply> [ID|PATH] [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Discover, inspect, or render native Steam Workshop (\fB431960\fR Wallpaper Engine) scenes, videos, web wallpapers, \fB.pkg\fR archives, \fB.tex\fR textures, \fB.mdl\fR Puppet Warp skeletal meshes, AVX2 particle systems, and \fBSceneScript\fR logic. Use \fB--prop key=val\fR to override user properties.
.RE
.PP
\fBslideshow\fR <DIR|ACTION> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Start a zero-idle-CPU \fBtimerfd\fR wallpaper slideshow from \fIDIR\fR, or control an active slideshow using one of the actions: \fBstart\fR, \fBstop\fR, \fBpause\fR, \fBresume\fR, \fBtoggle\fR, \fBnext\fR, \fBprev\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBcolor\fR <HEX> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Set the target output(s) to a solid RGB/RGBA hex color (for example, \fB#1e1e2e\fR or \fB1e1e2eff\fR) using \fBwp_single_pixel_buffer_v1\fR when supported by the compositor.
.RE
.PP
\fBclear\fR [HEX] [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Alias for \fBcolor\fR (defaults to \fB000000\fR if no color is given) for \fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility.
.RE
.PP
\fBtheme\fR <PATH> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Extract an OKLab/CAM16/HCT Material Design 3 palette from \fIPATH\fR in under 0.4 ms and write \fB~/.local/state/caelestia/scheme.json\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors.json\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors.css\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors-hyprland.conf\fR, and terminal OSC 4/10/11 sequences.
.RE
.PP
\fBaudio\fR [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Configure live wallpaper audio playback volume (\fB--volume 0.0..1.0\fR) and external application auto-ducking (\fB--mute-on-audio\fR / \fB--no-mute-on-audio\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBset-uniform\fR <NAME> <VALUES...>
.RS 4
Mutate a live shader uniform or Workshop user property (1 to 4 float values) without reloading the active scene.
.RE
.PP
\fBstatus\fR [--json]
.RS 4
Inspect connected outputs, active wallpaper/video/shader/Workshop paths, D-Bus MPRIS2 media metadata, and daemon telemetry.
.RE
.PP
\fBsubscribe\fR
.RS 4
Stream newline-delimited JSON events whenever wallpapers, themes, or media states change.
.RE
.PP
\fBpause\fR
.RS 4
Pause active video, animation, live shader, or Workshop scene playback.
.RE
.PP
\fBresume\fR, \fBunpause\fR
.RS 4
Resume paused video, animation, live shader, or Workshop scene playback.
.RE
.PP
\fBtoggle\fR
.RS 4
Toggle video, animation, live shader, or Workshop scene playback between paused and playing states.
.RE
.PP
\fBquery\fR [--json]
.RS 4
List all connected Wayland outputs, physical and logical dimensions, scale factors, refresh rates, and active wallpaper state.
.RE
.PP
\fBstats\fR [--json]
.RS 4
Query real-time daemon telemetry (opcode \fB0x000C\fR), including daemon RSS/PSS memory footprint, active VRAM surface pool count, negotiated DRM FourCC format and modifier (Linear, NVIDIA Block-Linear, ARM AFBC, AMD DCC, Intel CCS), VBlank PLL period/phase jitter estimates, and per-output Zero-Watt \fBpause_mask\fR reasons.
.RE
.PP
\fBrestore\fR
.RS 4
Restore the last persisted per-output wallpaper, video, shader, Workshop scene, or color state from \fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/wwal/state.bin\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBclear-cache\fR
.RS 4
Remove cached hardware-transcoded animations and palette artifacts from \fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/wwal\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBinit\fR
.RS 4
Launch or initialize the \fBwwald\fR(1) daemon (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility alias).
.RE
.PP
\fBping\fR
.RS 4
Check whether \fBwwald\fR(1) is running and responsive over the IPC socket.
.RE
.PP
\fBkill\fR
.RS 4
Gracefully terminate the running \fBwwald\fR(1) daemon.
.RE
.PP
\fBversion\fR
.RS 4
Print version information and exit.
.RE
.PP
\fBhelp\fR
.RS 4
Show command-line usage summary.
.RE
.PP
.SH IMAGE & TRANSITION OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--transition-type\fR <TYPE>
.RS 4
Select transition effect (default: \fBfade\fR). Supported GPU GLES 3.1 compute shader and AVX-512/AVX2/NEON SIMD transition types:
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnone\fR: Instant buffer swap with zero transition frames.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsimple\fR: Linear alpha cross-dissolve.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfade\fR: Cubic-bezier eased alpha crossfade.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwipe\fR: Directional linear edge wipe controlled by \fB--transition-angle\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgrow\fR: Expanding circular iris anchored at \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBouter\fR: Contracting circular iris toward \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwave\fR: Sinusoidal wave front controlled by \fB--transition-wave\fR and \fB--transition-angle\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnoise\fR: Perlin/simplex procedural noise dissolve.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcrosszoom\fR: Radial motion-blur zoom crossfade.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBslide\fR: Directional viewport push transition.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBglitch\fR: RGB chromatic aberration and block-shift digital glitch.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBburn\fR: Procedural ember/fire edge burn.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBripple\fR: Concentric water ripple refraction anchored at \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpixelate\fR: Dynamic mosaic block quantization transition.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdoom\fR: Classic vertical column melt transition.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBswirl\fR: Spiral vortex distortion around \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcube\fR: 3D perspective rotating cube face transition.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBluma\fR: Luminance threshold ramp transition.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlight_leak\fR: Warm filmic anamorphic flare transition.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpage_curl\fR: 3D cylindrical page curl with specular shading.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcustom\fR: User-supplied GLSL compute shader via \fB--transition-shader\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, \fBtop\fR, \fBbottom\fR: Directional slide transition aliases (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility).
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcenter\fR, \fBany\fR: Centered or arbitrary radial iris grow aliases (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility).
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrandom\fR: Randomly choose one of the 18 built-in shader transitions.
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-duration\fR <SECONDS>
.RS 4
Duration of the transition in seconds (default: \fB1.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-fps\fR <FPS>
.RS 4
Target transition frame rate (default: \fB60\fR; automatically locks to display VBlank via \fBwp_presentation\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-bezier\fR <X1,Y1,X2,Y2>
.RS 4
Cubic Bezier control points for transition progress easing (default: \fB0.25,0.1,0.25,1.0\fR; \fBswww\fR default: \fB0.54,0,0.34,0.99\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-angle\fR <DEGREES>
.RS 4
Direction angle in degrees for \fBwipe\fR, \fBwave\fR, and \fBslide\fR transitions (default: \fB0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-wave\fR <FREQ,AMP>
.RS 4
Frequency and amplitude for the \fBwave\fR transition (default: \fB20,0.05\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-pos\fR <POS>
.RS 4
Anchor position for \fBgrow\fR, \fBouter\fR, \fBripple\fR, and \fBswirl\fR transitions. Accepts normalized coordinates \fBX,Y\fR in \fB0.0..1.0\fR, or semantic aliases: \fBcenter\fR, \fBtop\fR, \fBbottom\fR, \fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, \fBtop-left\fR, \fBtop-right\fR, \fBbottom-left\fR, \fBbottom-right\fR, \fBcursor\fR, \fBmouse\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-step\fR <STEP>
.RS 4
Per-frame progress step (\fB1..255\fR) for \fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility.
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-shader\fR <FILE>
.RS 4
Path to a custom GLSL ES 3.10 compute shader (\fB.comp\fR) when \fB--transition-type custom\fR is selected.
.RE
.PP
\fB-o, --output, --outputs\fR <NAMES>
.RS 4
Target specific Wayland output(s) by name (for example, \fBDP-1\fR or \fBDP-1,HDMI-A-1\fR). May be specified multiple times.
.RE
.PP
\fB--sync-mode\fR <simultaneous|staggered>
.RS 4
Synchronize transitions across multiple monitors simultaneously or with a cascading delay (default: \fBsimultaneous\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--stagger-delay\fR <MS>
.RS 4
Cascading delay in milliseconds between outputs when \fB--sync-mode staggered\fR is active (default: \fB150\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--scaling-mode, --mode, --resize\fR <MODE>
.RS 4
Aspect-ratio scaling mode:
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfill\fR, \fBcrop\fR, \fBcover\fR: Scale to fill the entire output, cropping excess edges (default).
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfit\fR, \fBcontain\fR: Scale to fit inside the output, padding letterbox/pillarbox bars with \fB--fill-color\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstretch\fR: Stretch non-uniformly to output dimensions.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcenter\fR, \fBno\fR: Center at 1:1 pixel resolution, padding surrounding space with \fB--fill-color\fR.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtile\fR: Repeat image in a tiled grid across the output.
.RE
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBspan\fR: Span a single panoramic canvas across the combined logical layout of all active monitors.
.RE
.PP
\fB--depth-map\fR <FILE>
.RS 4
Enable interactive 3D Parallax Occlusion Mapping (POM) on a 2D image using the grayscale depth map at \fIFILE\fR, driven by smoothed cursor tracking and workspace-slide inertia.
.RE
.PP
\fB--depth-strength\fR <FLOAT>
.RS 4
Depth parallax displacement multiplier when \fB--depth-map\fR is active (default: \fB1.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--fill-color\fR <HEX>
.RS 4
Background padding color in 6- or 8-digit hex for \fBfit\fR and \fBcenter\fR modes (default: \fB000000\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--filter\fR <Nearest|Bilinear|CatmullRom|Mitchell|Lanczos3>
.RS 4
Sampling filter hint for image scaling (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility).
.RE
.PP
\fB--10bit\fR
.RS 4
Request 10-bit wide-gamut scanout (\fBDRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010\fR / \fBDRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010\fR) and preserve 16-bit PNG/AVIF/JXL channel precision when supported by the compositor.
.RE
.PP
\fB--backdrop\fR <none|auto-blur|FILE>
.RS 4
Configure a secondary layer-shell surface with namespace \fBwaywal-backdrop\fR for compositors with overview backdrops such as Niri (\fBplace-within-backdrop true\fR). \fBauto-blur\fR renders a 2-pass Dual-Kawase Gaussian blur of the active wallpaper on the GPU at zero extra image-decode cost.
.RE
.PP
\fB--layer\fR <background|bottom>
.RS 4
Wayland layer-shell layer placement (default: \fBbackground\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--theme, --no-theme\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable automatic Material Design 3 OKLab/CAM16/HCT color extraction and \fBcaelestia\fR/\fBOSC\fR synchronization on wallpaper change.
.RE
.PP
\fB--theme-from-media, --no-theme-from-media\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable dynamic Material Design 3 palette extraction from active D-Bus \fBMPRIS2\fR album art.
.RE
.PP
\fB--animate\fR
.RS 4
Route animated GIF/WebP/APNG files through the hardware video/animation engine.
.RE
.PP
.SH VIDEO, SHADER & POWER OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-p, --prop\fR <KEY=VALUE>
.RS 4
Override a Wallpaper Engine Workshop user property when applying a scene (repeatable).
.RE
.PP
\fB--loop\fR <COUNT>
.RS 4
Number of playback loops for \fBvideo\fR (\fB0\fR for infinite loop, default: \fB0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--speed\fR <MULTIPLIER>
.RS 4
Playback speed multiplier for \fBvideo\fR and \fBshader\fR (default: \fB1.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--fps\fR <FPS>
.RS 4
Target rendering frame rate for \fBshader\fR and \fBworkshop\fR scenes (default: \fB60\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--audio\fR
.RS 4
Enable lock-free PipeWire default sink monitor capture and 64-bin logarithmic Bark-scale FFT uniforms (\fBu_audio_bands[64]\fR, \fBu_audio_envelope\fR, and Shadertoy \fBiChannel0\fR 512x2 audio texture) for \fBshader\fR and \fBworkshop\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fB--volume\fR <0.0..1.0>
.RS 4
Set wallpaper audio playback volume for \fBvideo\fR, \fBshader\fR, \fBworkshop\fR, and \fBaudio\fR (default: \fB0.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--mute-on-audio, --no-mute-on-audio\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable automatic exponential volume ducking when another application plays audio via PipeWire.
.RE
.PP
\fB--battery-policy\fR <ignore|reduce-fps|pause-video>
.RS 4
Configure the laptop battery governor policy when discharging or entering power-saver mode.
.RE
.PP
.SH SLIDESHOW OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-d, --interval\fR <SECONDS>
.RS 4
Interval in seconds between slideshow transitions (default: \fB300\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB-s, --shuffle, --random\fR
.RS 4
Randomize slideshow traversal order using Fisher-Yates shuffling.
.RE
.PP
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR
.RS 4
Wayland compositor socket name.
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory containing the \fBwwald\fR(1) IPC socket (\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wwald.sock\fR or \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/$WAYLAND_DISPLAY-wwald.<namespace>.sock\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Location of \fBwwal/config.toml\fR (defaults to \fB~/.config\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Location of \fBwwal/\fR generated color schemes and cached transcodes (defaults to \fB~/.cache\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Location of \fBwwal/state.bin\fR persistent output state (defaults to \fB~/.local/state\fR).
.RE
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB~/.config/wwal/config.toml\fR
.RS 4
Declarative daemon, theme, transition, output, and workspace configuration. See \fBwwal-config\fR(5).
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.local/state/caelestia/scheme.json\fR
.RS 4
Material Design 3 tonal palette output for Quickshell (\fBcaelestia-shell\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.cache/wwal/colors.json\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors.css\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors-hyprland.conf\fR
.RS 4
Exported OKLab/HCT palette files for Waybar, GTK, and Hyprland.
.RE
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Set a wallpaper with a 144 FPS circular iris transition anchored at the cursor and extract a Material You palette:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal img ~/Pictures/cyberpunk.avif --transition-type grow --transition-pos cursor --transition-fps 144 --theme
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set a wallpaper with a Niri Dual-Kawase blurred overview backdrop and custom cubic-bezier curve:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal img ~/Pictures/mountain.jxl --backdrop auto-blur --transition-bezier 0.22,1.0,0.36,1.0
.RE
.fi
.PP
Play a 4K 60 FPS video wallpaper with zero-copy VA-API decoding:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal video ~/Videos/loop.mp4 --output DP-1
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run an audio-reactive Shadertoy wallpaper fed by PipeWire FFT:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal shader ~/Shaders/nebula.frag --audio
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inspect live DMA-BUF modifiers, VRAM pool usage, and Zero-Watt occlusion state:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal stats
.RE
.fi
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBwwald\fR(1), \fBwwal-config\fR(5)
